# Self-explaining code

JS/TS only. Leave `*.sh` and other non-JS/TS files untouched. Leave `${var#pattern}`, `${var##pattern}`, and `${#var}` whole — that `#` is a shell parameter expansion, not a comment.

Do not write or keep explanatory comments, commented-out code, HACK notes, or workaround excuses. Put intent in names, extracted functions, types, and tests. Fix workarounds or track them in an issue.

**Allowed only:** `TODO` / `FIXME`; license/SPDX headers; directives/pragmas with a reason (`eslint-disable`, `stylelint-disable`, `prettier-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, `'use client'`, `/* @__PURE__ */`, `/* glsl */`, beasties, `/// <reference>`, `fallow-ignore-next-line`); JSDoc on public exported APIs when the signature cannot carry the contract; a rare URL to an issue/spec for a constraint a name cannot hold.

Skill: `.agents/skills/no-code-comments`.
